    "updated_at": "2026-11-18T12:19:09Z",
    "body": "Claim released. STOPPED in Step 7 after `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` failed twice on the pre-existing `#2483` failure.\n\nWhat was verified:\n- Reproduction and fix: `grblhal_zero_dwell_g86_has_p0`, `tormach_zero_dwell_g86_has_p0`, and `canned_posts_write_g86_and_no_other_cycle` in `crates/post/tests/bore_cycle.rs` failed before the fix (`G86` emitted without `P0`). Changing the dwell guard in `assets/posts/grblhal.cps` and `assets/posts/tormach.cps` (`onCycle`) to `if (g === \"G86\" || (dwell > 0 && (g === \"G82\" || g === \"G89\")))` and adding `P0` to the `G86` blocks in `crates/post/tests/golden/bore/grblhal.nc` and `crates/post/tests/golden/bore/tormach.nc` makes all 9 tests in `camcraft-post --test bore_cycle` pass.\n- Mutation checks: restoring `upstream/main`'s `assets/posts/grblhal.cps` made `grblhal_zero_dwell_g86_has_p0` fail and restoring the fix made it pass; doing the same for `assets/posts/tormach.cps` made `tormach_zero_dwell_g86_has_p0` fail and restoring the fix made it pass.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`): 128 of 129 steps passed (all 89 `camcraft-post` steps and 38 of 39 `camcraft-app` steps); `app suites: microarc_test_part` failed (`a_wrapped_op_on_the_test_part_posts_wrapped_a`, `wrap_rotary_parallel_microarc4.nc: line count 3246 != 3245`). Re-running `--failed` failed identically, and testing with unmodified `upstream/main` `assets/posts/tormach.cps` (`2c789ed6d`) failed identically — this is the open `main is red` defect tracked in #2483, unrelated to G86.\n- Overlap check: PR #2346 touches `assets/posts/tormach.cps` (`onCycle` `motionFor`, already on `upstream/main` via #2386, not the `P`-word guard); PR #2506 touches `crates/post/tests/bore_cycle.rs` (`EXPANDED` array only).\n\nNo PR was opened and nothing was pushed. Held patch remains locally in `/home/mikekinney/Camcraft/.claude/worktrees/issue-2362` on branch `issue/2362-g86-zero-dwell` (branched from `2c789ed6d`) so it can be re-gated once #2483 lands on `main`.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
